e cost management.\n* Coordinate with housekeeping, front office, food and beverage, maintenance, and other relevant departments.\n* Conduct regular inspections of guest areas and operational facilities.\n* Maintain appropriate operational records and prepare reports for management.\n* Coordinate with suppliers and service providers when required.\n* Support management in implementing initiatives to improve guest satisfaction and operational efficiency.\n* Ensure relevant health, safety, and security procedures are followed.\n\nRequirements\n\n* Diploma or bachelor's degree in Hotel Management, Hospitality, Business Administration, or a related field.\n* Previous experience in hotel or hospitality operations.\n* Experience managing or supervising a hotel operations team is preferred.\n* Good communication and interpersonal skills.\n* Strong organizational and problem\\-solving abilities.\n* Ability to manage multiple operational priorities.\n* Customer\\-focused approach with professional conduct.\n* Basic knowledge of hotel PMS and Microsoft Office applications is preferred.\n\nPay: \u20b930,381\\.73 \\- \u20b958,743\\.89 per month\n\nBenefits:\n\n* Flexible schedule\n* Food provided\n\nAbility to commute/relocate:\n\n* Kolkata, West Bengal: Reliably commute or planning to relocate before starting work (Required)\n\nEducation:\n\n* Diploma (Required)\n\nExperience:\n\n* Hotel management: 4 years (Required)\n\nWork Location: In person","indeed_jk":"d40e9b380b77bd84","permanent_url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=d40e9b380b77bd84&from=serp&vjs=3"}]